<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends steady in a quiet market.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends steady in a quiet market.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The taka closed steady at 42.5470/5495 to the dollar in interbank trading, against the previous 42.5470/5490, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the taka quoted easier at 42.4375/5495 in early trade and remained almost at that level in yet another quiet session.</p>
<p>Deals were worth about $5 million.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates finished flat at 4.5 percent to 5.5 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom  +880-2-506363</p>
</text>
